WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.083
<b>In the previous verse, we understood</b>

3
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:34.875
<b>that raag means excessive attraction,</b>

4
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:37.916
<b>and dvesh means excessive aversion.</b>

5
00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:41.041
<b>Humans should stay away from both.</b>

6
00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.666
<b>But consider -</b>

7
00:00:42.666 --> 00:00:44.166
<b>Arjuna is a warrior,</b>

8
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:45.875
<b>he must fight battles,</b>

9
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.875
<b>protect the kingdom,</b>

10
00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:50.416
<b>and destroy enemies.</b>

11
00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:55.875
<b>His mind might say this isn't possible </b>
<b>without attachment and aversion...</b>

12
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:56.875
<b>And for this reason,</b>

13
00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:59.458
<b>if he must abandon attachment and aversion,</b>

14
00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.333
<b>he would have to leave his warrior duty</b>

15
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:06.958
<b>and adopt the life of a monk </b>
<b>or complete non-violence.</b>

16
00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:09.666
<b>The human mind is very clever,</b>

17
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:13.416
<b>capable of presenting many </b>
<b>arguments to stray from duty.</b>

18
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:16.791
<b>This verse answers such dilemmas.</b>

19
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:21.666


20
00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:24.416
<b>Lord Krishna says in this verse</b>

21
00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:27.708
<b>that performing one's own duties imperfectly</b>

22
00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:32.291
<b>is better than excellently </b>
<b>performing another's duties.</b>

23
00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>Following others' duties is dangerous,</b>

24
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:42.791
<b>while death in performing one's own duty is noble.</b>

25
00:01:42.791 --> 00:01:50.875
<b>Krishna explains to Arjuna how crucial it is for</b>
<b>humans to stay true to their dharma.</b>

26
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:51.583
<b>Here,</b>

27
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:58.250
<b>dharma means the duty assigned </b>
<b>according to one's natural disposition.</b>

28
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.000
<b>Even if difficulties arise in following one's dharma,</b>

29
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.583
<b>one should remain steadfast on this path.</b>

30
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.041
<b>But why?</b>

31
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:12.208
<b>Why does Krishna say that </b>
<b>performing one's duties imperfectly</b>

32
00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:16.250
<b>is better than excellently </b>
<b>performing another's duties?</b>

33
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:25.000
<b>Attraction towards others' duties typically </b>
<b>arises when one faces difficulties in their own.</b>

34
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.208
<b>At such times,</b>

35
00:02:26.208 --> 00:02:31.666
<b>it seems that if we can perform </b>
<b>someone else's duty well,</b>

36
00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:34.166
<b>why not change paths?</b>

37
00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:35.500
<b>In the first chapter,</b>

38
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.541
<b>Arjuna too said</b>

39
00:02:37.541 --> 00:02:43.000
<b>that instead of this war, he would rather</b>
<b>live as a mendicant in the forest.</b>

40
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.125
<b>At such times,</b>

41
00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:50.541
<b>we only see the simplicity of others' duties,</b>
<b>not their complexities.</b>

42
00:02:50.541 --> 00:02:51.875
<b>For example,</b>

43
00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:57.166
<b>Arjuna found a mendicant's </b>
<b>duty easier than this war.</b>

44
00:02:57.166 --> 00:03:02.333
<b>Perhaps initially Arjuna could </b>
<b>perform this duty well,</b>

45
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:05.208
<b>but would it last?</b>

46
00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:08.083
<b>A mendicant's life includes facing rejection.</b>

47
00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:13.458
<b>What if someone closes their door or </b>
<b>insults them while begging?</b>

48
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:17.875
<b>In such situations, a natural </b>
<b>mendicant would endure,</b>

49
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:24.666
<b>but could a warrior like </b>
<b>Arjuna tolerate such insults?</b>

50
00:03:24.666 --> 00:03:25.583
<b>No.</b>

51
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:30.375
<b>After some time, he would grow </b>
<b>to hate that new life.</b>

52
00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:34.708
<b>While war may be much harder than begging,</b>

53
00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:39.875
<b>a warrior like Arjuna has a natural disposition</b>
<b>towards valor and prowess.</b>

54
00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:45.833
<b>And if Arjuna attains a warrior's </b>
<b>death fighting for dharma,</b>

55
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:50.416
<b>he would achieve heaven for fulfilling his duty.</b>

56
00:03:50.416 --> 00:03:51.208
<b>Therefore,</b>

57
00:03:51.208 --> 00:03:52.833
<b>scriptures teach that</b>

58
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:59.708
<b>humans should wholeheartedly follow duties </b>
<b>aligned with their natural tendencies.</b>

59
00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:00.583
<b>This way,</b>

60
00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:03.166
<b>they gradually purify themselves</b>

61
00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:06.833
<b>and achieve spiritual progress.</b>

62
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.958
<b>Just as Arjuna cannot become a mendicant,</b>

63
00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:14.458
<b>similarly a mendicant, </b>
<b>who is gentle and non-violent,</b>

64
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:17.333
<b>could they fight on a battlefield?</b>

65
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:18.583
<b>No.</b>

66
00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:23.333
<b>Can a person with business </b>
<b>tendencies become a warrior?</b>

67
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:24.083
<b>No.</b>

68
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:27.416
<b>Because in war, financial gain is minimal,</b>

69
00:04:27.416 --> 00:04:28.333
<b>but</b>

70
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:31.291
<b>one might pay with their life.</b>

71
00:04:31.291 --> 00:04:36.500
<b>This contradicts the business</b>
<b>mindset of economic profit.</b>

72
00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.166
<b>Everyone is important,</b>

73
00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:41.041
<b>each has their unique place.</b>

74
00:04:41.041 --> 00:04:47.541
<b>Sometimes, seeing momentary difficulties,</b>
<b>humans think others' duties are easier.</b>

75
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.375
<b>Everyone's duty is different.</b>

76
00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:53.041
<b>Ease and complexity depend on disposition.</b>

77
00:04:53.041 --> 00:04:56.875
<b>A mathematically inclined</b>
<b>student finds math easy,</b>

78
00:04:56.875 --> 00:05:01.333
<b>while an art lover might find it complex.</b>

79
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.000
<b>One must recognize their specialty,</b>

80
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.250
<b>know their disposition,</b>

81
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:12.958
<b>choose duties accordingly, and </b>
<b>then focus on their work.</b>

82
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:16.375
<b>Challenges will naturally arise,</b>

83
00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:20.166
<b>but being on the path of their natural tendency,</b>

84
00:05:20.166 --> 00:05:24.833
<b>they will handle these </b>
<b>challenges better than others.</b>

85
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:29.250


86
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:35.958
<b>A challenging path aligned with your true nature</b>

87
00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:41.166
<b>is far better than an unnatural </b>
<b>one that seems easy.</b>

88
00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:43.916
<b> Think of those moments</b>

89
00:05:43.916 --> 00:05:44.833
<b>when</b>

90
00:05:44.833 --> 00:05:51.541
<b>when you saw someone and </b>
<b>wished you were in their shoes,</b>

91
00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:56.458
<b>doing what they do.</b>

92
00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:57.958
<b>For instance,</b>

93
00:05:57.958 --> 00:06:05.500
<b>you might have seen a travel expert </b>
<b>who visits various destinations,</b>

94
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.958
<b>stays at new places every week,</b>

95
00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:11.458
<b>and appears joyful.</b>

96
00:06:11.458 --> 00:06:13.875
<b>'How exciting this work must be,'</b>

97
00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:20.166
<b>you thought. 'If only I had such a job, </b>
<b>I'd be so happy.'</b>

98
00:06:20.166 --> 00:06:24.416
<b>Such thoughts must have crossed your mind,</b>

99
00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:26.875
<b>haven't they?</b>

100
00:06:26.875 --> 00:06:29.750
<b>While these thoughts are inspiring,</b>

101
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:42.333
<b>one often forgets to weigh whether such </b>
<b>work truly aligns with their nature.</b>

102
00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:49.625
<b>That travel expert can't stay at one place </b>
<b>for more than a day or two,</b>

103
00:06:49.625 --> 00:06:58.458
<b>he can't relax as it is his work, and not a vacation.</b>

104
00:06:58.458 --> 00:07:02.958
<b>They constantly live away from home.</b>

105
00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:04.041
<b>And</b>

106
00:07:04.041 --> 00:07:09.666
<b>You don't even know their financial stability.</b>

107
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:18.541
<b>Being drawn to another's duty is like </b>
<b>wearing someone else's beautiful shoes.</b>

108
00:07:18.541 --> 00:07:23.875
<b>They might look appealing and feel good briefly,</b>

109
00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:24.791
<b>but</b>

110
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:34.541
<b>if they don't fit your feet, </b>
<b>you'll soon develop blisters.</b>

111
00:07:34.541 --> 00:07:36.916
<b>You must choose shoes</b>

112
00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:41.041
<b>that fit your feet perfectly.</b>

113
00:07:41.041 --> 00:07:44.166
<b>The ease or complexity of work,</b>

114
00:07:44.166 --> 00:07:46.708
<b>its pleasures and pains,</b>

115
00:07:46.708 --> 00:07:49.750
<b>don't depend solely on the work itself.</b>

116
00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:58.708
<b>Rather, they depend on how well </b>
<b>that work aligns with your nature.</b>

117
00:07:58.708 --> 00:08:01.625
<b>Indifference towards your duty</b>

118
00:08:01.625 --> 00:08:10.166
<b>typically arises when you face </b>
<b>challenges on your chosen path.</b>

119
00:08:10.166 --> 00:08:13.500
<b>Challenges will come on every path –</b>

120
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.125
<b>this is the test of your resolve.</b>

121
00:08:18.125 --> 00:08:20.125
<b>Remember,</b>

122
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:26.583
<b>overcoming such tests not only </b>
<b>brings immense satisfaction</b>

123
00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:27.666
<b>but</b>

124
00:08:27.666 --> 00:08:31.375
<b>also enhances your skills and understanding.</b>

125
00:08:31.375 --> 00:08:33.458
<b>Think –</b>

126
00:08:33.458 --> 00:08:40.041
<b>was your current position easily achieved?</b>

127
00:08:40.041 --> 00:08:41.833
<b>No, right?</b>

128
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:48.208
<b>It was through challenges that you </b>
<b>learned and grew more capable.</b>

129
00:08:48.208 --> 00:08:50.458
<b>The essence is...</b>

130
00:08:50.458 --> 00:08:54.791
<b>don't be attracted to others' duties.</b>

131
00:08:54.791 --> 00:08:59.500
<b>Instead, understand your natural inclinations</b>

132
00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:04.750
<b>and choose your path accordingly.</b>

133
00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:09.541
<b>This path will not only bring inner satisfaction</b>

134
00:09:09.541 --> 00:09:10.541
<b>but</b>

135
00:09:10.541 --> 00:09:16.916
<b>will also lead you toward a </b>
<b>meaningful and purposeful life.</b>

136
00:09:17.458 --> 00:09:21.416


137
00:09:21.416 --> 00:09:25.833
<b>Imagine a family</b>

138
00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:28.333
<b>where each member</b>

139
00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:37.583
<b>is encouraged to choose paths aligned</b>
<b>with their natural personality and abilities.</b>

140
00:09:37.583 --> 00:09:45.166
<b>Where no one is pressured to choose paths</b>
<b>that contradict their true nature.</b>

141
00:09:45.166 --> 00:09:47.041
<b>In such a family,</b>

142
00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:51.083
<b>not only does everyone feel respected,</b>

143
00:09:51.083 --> 00:09:52.125
<b>but</b>

144
00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:58.000
<b>they also progress because they're working </b>
<b>according to their natural inclinations</b>

145
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:03.750
<b>and live contentedly.</b>

146
00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.416
<b>Often, parents,</b>

147
00:10:05.416 --> 00:10:08.125
<b>without understanding their children's interests,</b>

148
00:10:08.125 --> 00:10:13.416
<b>pressure them to choose a path</b>

149
00:10:13.416 --> 00:10:20.291
<b>that perhaps they themselves </b>
<b>wanted but couldn't achieve.</b>

150
00:10:20.291 --> 00:10:25.500
<b>Sometimes, it's the pressure</b>
<b>of social expectations.</b>

151
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.416
<b>If you're a parent,</b>

152
00:10:28.416 --> 00:10:32.708
<b>look within and ask yourself –</b>

153
00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:38.041
<b>if your child chooses a path under pressure,</b>

154
00:10:38.041 --> 00:10:43.583
<b>will they remain happy years from now?</b>

155
00:10:43.583 --> 00:10:44.916
<b>Naturally,</b>

156
00:10:44.916 --> 00:10:49.166
<b>parents want the best for their children,</b>

157
00:10:49.166 --> 00:10:51.708
<b>but instead of pressure,</b>

158
00:10:51.708 --> 00:10:54.250
<b>use collaborative discussion.</b>

159
00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.416
<b>Weigh both sides' arguments impartially,</b>

160
00:10:57.416 --> 00:11:03.083
<b>and if your child still wants </b>
<b>to follow their chosen path,</b>

161
00:11:03.083 --> 00:11:04.875
<b>support them.</b>

162
00:11:04.875 --> 00:11:08.125
<b>Give them their time.</b>

163
00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:11.791
<b>If your child succeeds,</b>

164
00:11:11.791 --> 00:11:15.208
<b>their confidence will grow.</b>

165
00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:19.375
<b>If later they find your advice was right,</b>

166
00:11:19.375 --> 00:11:23.833
<b>they'll learn a life lesson.</b>

167
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:27.791
<b>Sometimes, by willingly taking the wrong path,</b>

168
00:11:27.791 --> 00:11:32.208
<b>one learns the wisdom to choose the right one.</b>

169
00:11:32.208 --> 00:11:34.500
<b>The Gita teaches us</b>

170
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:40.583
<b>that we must recognize the natural </b>
<b>inclinations of each family member</b>

171
00:11:40.583 --> 00:11:46.750
<b>and encourage them to </b>
<b>choose their duty accordingly.</b>

172
00:11:47.208 --> 00:11:50.958


173
00:11:50.958 --> 00:11:53.416
<b>In a professional environment,</b>

174
00:11:53.416 --> 00:11:58.583
<b>when we compare our work with others,</b>

175
00:11:58.583 --> 00:12:02.833
<b>we sometimes feel dissatisfied.</b>

176
00:12:02.833 --> 00:12:11.250
<b>Sometimes it feels like others have moved</b>
<b>ahead while we've fallen behind.</b>

177
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.000
<b>But think –</b>

178
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.250
<b>the person you consider ahead of you,</b>

179
00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:23.666
<b>isn't there someone ahead of them too?</b>

180
00:12:23.666 --> 00:12:27.083
<b>Such comparison is endless.</b>

181
00:12:27.083 --> 00:12:29.791
<b>The Gita teaches that</b>

182
00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:31.958
<b>instead of comparison,</b>

183
00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:36.166
<b>we should focus on our work.</b>

184
00:12:36.166 --> 00:12:39.000
<b>Find joy in it.</b>

185
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:47.125
<b>And this joy comes when our work and</b>
<b>responsibilities align with our nature.</b>

186
00:12:47.125 --> 00:12:49.125
<b>For example,</b>

187
00:12:49.125 --> 00:12:56.791
<b>if someone enjoys interacting with people </b>
<b>and is sensitive to others' problems,</b>

188
00:12:56.791 --> 00:13:01.541
<b>they'll find more satisfaction in customer service</b>

189
00:13:01.541 --> 00:13:06.875
<b>than sitting alone analyzing numbers.</b>

190
00:13:06.875 --> 00:13:13.666
<b>Success isn't measured solely by </b>
<b>promotions or financial progress.</b>

191
00:13:13.666 --> 00:13:16.500
<b>Like any aspect of life,</b>

192
00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:21.708
<b>the true measure of success in professional life is</b>

193
00:13:21.708 --> 00:13:24.583
<b>self-satisfaction.</b>

194
00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:26.958
<b>For this self-satisfaction,</b>

195
00:13:26.958 --> 00:13:31.416
<b>choose professional duties </b>
<b>according to your nature.</b>

196
00:13:31.416 --> 00:13:32.916
<b>Also,</b>

197
00:13:32.916 --> 00:13:39.666
<b>if you lead a team, remember these three things:</b>

198
00:13:39.666 --> 00:13:41.000
<b>First –</b>

199
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.250
<b>Everyone is special;</b>

200
00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:48.500
<b>recognize their uniqueness and utilize it well.</b>

201
00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.750
<b>Second –</b>

202
00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:54.333
<b>Support your colleagues' personal goals.</b>

203
00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:55.291
<b>Third –</b>

204
00:13:55.291 --> 00:13:59.083
<b>Celebrate their every victory enthusiastically.</b>

205
00:13:59.083 --> 00:14:03.250
<b>In such a workplace atmosphere,</b>

206
00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:09.166
<b>instead of competition, everyone will work </b>
<b>to their full potential.</b>

207
00:14:09.166 --> 00:14:12.791
<b>Everyone will support each other.</b>

208
00:14:12.791 --> 00:14:18.666
<b>Whether you work individually </b>
<b>or in a leadership position,</b>

209
00:14:18.666 --> 00:14:20.583
<b>remember:</b>

210
00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:27.208
<b>Mind compares only when </b>
<b>self-satisfaction is missing.</b>

211
00:14:27.208 --> 00:14:30.583
<b>And the sure path to self-satisfaction is</b>

212
00:14:30.583 --> 00:14:36.750
<b>walking the path chosen according</b>
<b>to your preferences and inclinations.</b>

213
00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.583
<b>Think about it.</b>

